## Overview

This document defines MedSync's incident management process for production incidents affecting platform availability, performance, or security.

---

## Incident Classification

### Severity Levels

| Severity | Definition | Examples |
|----------|------------|----------|
| SEV1 - Critical | Major outage affecting all customers | Platform down, data breach |
| SEV2 - Major | Significant degradation or partial outage | Core feature unavailable |
| SEV3 - Minor | Limited impact, workaround available | Single integration failure |
| SEV4 - Low | Minimal impact, scheduled maintenance | Non-critical alert |

### Classification Criteria

| Factor | SEV1 | SEV2 | SEV3 | SEV4 |
|--------|------|------|------|------|
| Customer Impact | All | Many | Some | Few |
| Revenue Impact | High | Medium | Low | None |
| Data at Risk | Yes | Possible | No | No |
| SLA Breach | Certain | Likely | Possible | No |
| Media Risk | High | Medium | Low | None |

