## Incident Workflow

### Phase 1: Detection (0-5 min)

| Step | Action | Owner |
|------|--------|-------|
| 1 | Alert triggered or report received | Automated/Anyone |
| 2 | Acknowledge alert | On-call |
| 3 | Initial assessment | On-call |
| 4 | Declare incident severity | On-call + Manager |
| 5 | Create incident channel | IC |

### Phase 2: Response (5-30 min)

| Step | Action | Owner |
|------|--------|-------|
| 6 | Assemble response team | IC |
| 7 | Begin investigation | Technical Lead |
| 8 | Implement immediate mitigation | Technical Lead |
| 9 | Post initial customer update | Communications |
| 10 | Notify stakeholders | IC |

### Phase 3: Resolution (Ongoing)

| Step | Action | Owner |
|------|--------|-------|
| 11 | Root cause identification | Technical Lead |
| 12 | Implement fix | Engineering |
| 13 | Verify resolution | QA/On-call |
| 14 | Monitor stability | On-call |
| 15 | Customer communication | Communications |

### Phase 4: Closure (Post-resolution)

| Step | Action | Owner |
|------|--------|-------|
| 16 | Confirm stability (15+ min) | Technical Lead |
| 17 | Close incident channel | IC |
| 18 | Final customer update | Communications |
| 19 | Schedule postmortem | IC |
| 20 | Log incident | Scribe |

